      "id": 1,
      "text": "Helvetia was founded in 1869 by Swiss immigrants after the Civil War, when West Virginia was still new.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://wvexplorer.com/helvetia-west-virginia-swiss/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Helvetia keeps Swiss traditions alive, hosting an annual Fasnacht celebration that blends Swiss Fasnacht and Sechseläuten customs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helvetia%2C_West_Virginia",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 100‑acre center was divided into lots sold to skilled tradesmen, encouraging craftsmen to settle.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
